    <string name="fix_paid">Paid, not connected</string>
    <string name="fix_still">Still not working? Tell us</string>
    <string-array name="fix_no_internet_steps">
        <item>Check that your plan is active on Home. An expired plan stops the internet until you renew.</item>
        <item>Look at the router: its lights should be on, and the internet or WAN light should not be red.</item>
        <item>Switch the router off at the plug, wait 30 seconds, and switch it back on. Give it two minutes.</item>
        <item>Check that the cable into the router is pushed in firmly at both ends.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="fix_slow_steps">
        <item>Open Usage. If you are past your plan\'s fair-usage amount, the speed is lower until it resets.</item>
        <item>Restart the router: off at the plug for 30 seconds, then on again.</item>
        <item>Move closer to the router, or use a cable. Walls and distance slow Wi-Fi down.</item>
        <item>Pause big downloads and updates on other phones, TVs and laptops.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="fix_paid_steps">
        <item>Open Payments and check that the payment is there. If it is, your plan is renewed.</item>
        <item>Restart the router so it connects again with the renewed plan.</item>
        <item>Still nothing after two minutes? Tell us here with the M-Pesa message, and we will check it.</item>
    </string-array>
